ree, with the numbers representing the height.  For example, the subtree ro=
oted at node '2' has a height of 2, and the subtree rooted at node '7' has =
a height of 2. Node '7' is highlighted in red.  To the right of the tree, t=
he text 'left_height =3D 0, right_height =3D 2' indicates the heights of th=
e left and right subtrees of node '5'.  The text 'height difference =3D 2 >=
 1 =E2=86=92 imbalanced' shows the calculation of the height difference (2 =
